     <target value="Spanish 2006: basic 68.4%, intermediate 23.0%, pro"></target>
     <actual value="Results for 4th grade: Spanish 2009: basic 63%, in">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary education curriculum was changed in 2007.  The Ministry of Education decided to collect a new student learningassessment baseline in grades 4th, 6th and 9th. The tests carried out in 2009 are not comparable with the baseline established in2002 for student achievements in Spanish and Math.  Results show a large percentage of students achieving the intermediate andproficient levels in both Spanish and mathematics in fourth grade. Although this is not comparable, it is at least an indicationthat students are meeting the learning standards of the new curriculum.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
